# Assessing Conversational Cognition: Levels of Cognitive Theory and Associated Methodological Requirements.

**Authors:** Waldron, Vincent R., Cegala, Donald J.

## Abstract
Suggests that claims about cognition can be made at four levels--biological, implementation, algorithmic, and rational--but that theoretical claims about conversational cognition can most usefully be pursued at the rational and algorithmic levels. Proposes criteria and reviews promising methods for studying conversational cognition, in an effort to promote more research at these levels. (SR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ445684

